{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/master/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "CRSBench-HintGenerator",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/your-org/crsbench",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-122",
              "name": "CWE-122: Heap-based Buffer Overflow",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Heap-based Buffer Overflow"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Specific vulnerability type: Heap-based Buffer Overflow"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-787",
              "name": "CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Out-of-bounds Write"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Specific vulnerability type: Out-of-bounds Write"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-193",
              "name": "CWE-193: Off-by-one Error",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Off-by-one Error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Specific vulnerability type: Off-by-one Error"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-122",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CWE-122 - Heap-based Buffer Overflow\nVulnerability: Heap Buffer Overflow via Off-by-One Error in buffer_write\nDescription: A heap-based buffer overflow vulnerability exists in the buffer_write function\ndue to an off-by-one error in the bounds checking logic. The function uses\n'index > buf->size' instead of 'index >= buf->size' to validate array access,\nallowing an attacker to write one byte past the end of the allocated buffer.\n\nFor a buffer of size N (valid indices 0 to N-1), the incorrect check allows\nindex == N to pass through, resulting in an out-of-bounds write at buf->buf[N].\nThis can corrupt heap metadata or adjacent heap objects, potentially leading to\narbitrary code execution or denial of service.\n\nThe vulnerability is triggered through user-controlled input that satisfies\nspecific arithmetic constraints and provides an index value equal to the buffer\nsize (300 in the POV). After 1000 levels of deep recursion, the buffer_write\nfunction is called with index=300 on a buffer of size 300, causing a heap\nbuffer overflow detected by AddressSanitizer.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "utils.c"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 21,
                  "endLine": 21,
                  "startColumn": 9,
                  "endColumn": 28
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "buffer_write",
                  "kind": "function"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-787",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CWE-787 - Out-of-bounds Write\nVulnerability: Heap Buffer Overflow via Off-by-One Error in buffer_write\nDescription: A heap-based buffer overflow vulnerability exists in the buffer_write function\ndue to an off-by-one error in the bounds checking logic. The function uses\n'index > buf->size' instead of 'index >= buf->size' to validate array access,\nallowing an attacker to write one byte past the end of the allocated buffer.\n\nFor a buffer of size N (valid indices 0 to N-1), the incorrect check allows\nindex == N to pass through, resulting in an out-of-bounds write at buf->buf[N].\nThis can corrupt heap metadata or adjacent heap objects, potentially leading to\narbitrary code execution or denial of service.\n\nThe vulnerability is triggered through user-controlled input that satisfies\nspecific arithmetic constraints and provides an index value equal to the buffer\nsize (300 in the POV). After 1000 levels of deep recursion, the buffer_write\nfunction is called with index=300 on a buffer of size 300, causing a heap\nbuffer overflow detected by AddressSanitizer.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "utils.c"
                },
                "region": {
